now how about the mathematics behind  this idea well you may not understand  all the symbols but just to kind of see  what it looks like we wrote down  equations physicists wrote down  equations way back 60s and 70s that were  wonderfully accurate at describing the  forces of nature the non gravitational  force is the electromagnetic force the  weak and strong nuclear forces we've  also written down equations that  describe the particles of matter in  which those forces act like electrons  and neutrinos and quarks the puzzling  thing is this those equations have built  in a fantastic amount of symmetry what I  mean by symmetry is from everyday life  if you have a snowflake  if you rotate that snowflake in the  right way it looks the same even though  you've rotated you've transformed it it  has symmetry if you take a sphere that's  even more symmetric as you rotate a  sphere regardless of what angle you  rotate it through it looks the same  similarly the basic equations had a  built-in symmetry much like that if you  mixed up the pieces of the equations  somehow it all coalesced that the  overall mathematical form stayed the  same the problem was if you wanted to  give mass to the matter particles or  even some of the force carrying  particles we knew how to do that  mathematically but the new mathematical  term looks like this it has a side bar  and a sign at that term if you brought  that into the equations ruin the  symmetry symmetry was shattered  completely went away and without the  symmetry the equations were actually  inconsistent they didn't work any longer  so the mathematical puzzle was to try to  give mass to the particles but not  destroy the symmetry the idea of Higgs  and various others was introduce a new  term one that didn't quite look like a  mass term at first sight one that was  completely symmetric like the others  when you brought this new term into the  equations the equations maintain their  beautiful symmetry but notice that  if that first factor in front of sidebar  side we call it Phi that symbol sitting  in front if that is re-written as say M  plus h where M is just a number then  when you multiply that through look what  happens the M multiplies the sidebar on  the site looks like a mass term and that  M is the constant value of the field  that's permeating space so that  permeating field in this mathematical  guise gives rise to the mass of  particles that's how the mathematical  form of this idea works
 

